import{_ as e,o as t,c as o,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 963 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 29 | Civilizational-Weight Assessment","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 963 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 29 | Civilizational-Weight Assessment","no":963,"module":5,"tags":["Heavenly-Dao Rule","Rule 29","Civilizational Weight","Assessment","Governance"],"related":["29-Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System","918-Civilizational-Weight Assessment System","964-Law-Anchor Permission Universalization"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0963_模块5-规则二十九-文明权重评估.md","filePath":"en/0963_模块5-规则二十九-文明权重评估.md"}'),n={name:"en/0963_模块5-规则二十九-文明权重评估.md"};function s(l,i,r,h,c,u){return t(),o("div",null,[...i[0]||(i[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-963-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-29-civilizational-weight-assessment" tabindex="-1">Entry 963 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 29 | Civilizational-Weight Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-963-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-29-civilizational-weight-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 963 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 29 | Civilizational-Weight Assessment&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Document 29 | Series: Complete Collection of Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-who-has-the-say-depends-on-contribution-not-voice-volume" tabindex="-1">Introduction: who has the say depends on contribution, not voice volume <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-who-has-the-say-depends-on-contribution-not-voice-volume" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: who has the say depends on contribution, not voice volume&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Governing a cross-plane, cross-Myriad-Rank civilization must answer a question: in major decisions, which civilization&#39;s opinion carries more weight? The old cosmos&#39;s answer is &quot;the strong decide&quot; — whoever has the bigger fist has the higher weight. Heavenly-Dao Rule 29 gives a new answer: civilizational weight is determined by that civilization&#39;s actual contribution to Myriad-Rank symbiosis, not by its military might, long history, or loud voice. A civilization quietly doing incremental development and lifting weak clans may carry more weight than an old stronghold sitting on heavy armies. This is the republican axiom of Myriad Races&#39; landing on &quot;say&#39;s allocation.&quot;</p><p>The six top-level axioms allocate say here: the republican axiom of Myriad Races is this rule&#39;s body; the collective-ascension axiom decides weight should flow to civilizations that do more &quot;lifting Myriad Ranks&quot;; the anti-predation axiom negates &quot;might equals weight&quot;; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the assessment process be fair and appealable; the law-first axiom lets &quot;assessment dimensions, calculation methods, rise-fall mechanisms&quot; be stipulated first by law; Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law sets a &quot;floor guarantee&quot; for weight — even an easygoing civilization or one unwilling to superimpose infinity retains a basic weight and is not completely kicked off the decision table for &quot;not striving enough.&quot;</p><h2 id="i-rule-content-civilizational-weight-assessment-dimensions" tabindex="-1">I. Rule Content: Civilizational-Weight Assessment Dimensions <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-rule-content-civilizational-weight-assessment-dimensions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Rule Content: Civilizational-Weight Assessment Dimensions&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Weight is calculated across four dimensions:</p><ol><li><strong>Increment-development contribution</strong> (highest weight): how many unlit law nodes this civilization has developed, how much public increment it has built;</li><li><strong>Lift-Myriad-Ranks contribution</strong>: how many weak clans, Youth Supremes, and newly incorporated civilizations it has helped;</li><li><strong>Rule-abiding record</strong>: whether it has long abided by Heavenly-Dao rules, any constitutional-violation record;</li><li><strong>Ecological contribution</strong>: positive impact on plane ecology and causal-network health.</li></ol><p>Weight is not lifetime: quarterly assessment, dynamic rise-fall; easygoing civilizations do not pursue high weight, but retain basic weight and a basic seat.</p><h2 id="ii-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">II. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Symbiosis-degree argument</strong>: the Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System (Document 29) proves a civilization&#39;s contribution to the network is quantifiable and comparable;</li><li><strong>Anti-strong-equals-truth argument</strong>: the old cosmos&#39;s &quot;might equals say&quot; is precisely predatory systems&#39; political expression; switching weight to contribution removes the fuel from the bottom;</li><li><strong>Floor-weight argument</strong>: under Axiom 6, easygoing civilizations inherently possess basic infinite power and retain floor participation rights, not losing their seat for not striving.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-execution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Execution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-execution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Execution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The Alaya Network automatically calculates a weight score for each civilization, with a dashboard open to all Myriad Ranks;</li><li>In major decisions, weight affects the size of its voting right, but everyone has a basic seat;</li><li>The entire weight rise-fall process is traced, and demoted civilizations may appeal;</li><li>No civilization may long top the chart: a &quot;weight rotation reminder&quot; is set, preventing weight from solidifying into a new class (connecting Rule 19).</li></ul><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Light</strong>: weight data lagging, update within a time limit;</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: forging contribution, grinding weight, relevant weight cleared to zero, responsible persons enter the conversion program;</li><li><strong>Heavy</strong>: using weight as leverage, manipulating weight calculation, handled heavily under Rule 5 (no private hoarding, no monopoly).</li></ul><h2 id="v-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">V. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s weight dashboard is the first layer; the Anchor Supervisory Committee verifies weight authenticity as the second layer; the Symbiotic Court adjudicates weight appeals as the third layer; lower-weight civilizations retain a direct channel to petition the Anchor Council as the fourth layer.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: giving say to civilizations with truly large contributions avoids decision-making idling from &quot;strong ones loud-voiced but low-contribution&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: negating might equals weight; under Axiom 6 easygoing civilizations also have a floor seat and do not speak by fists</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type systems&#39; say follows the protagonist halo; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s say follows symbiotic contribution</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the five lineages, easygoing and strivers, new and old civilizations are all in the assessment system</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: newly incorporated civilizations automatically gain basic weight, growing with contribution</li></ul><p>Civilizational-weight assessment must also guard against a new bias: with higher weight, will it become new privilege again? Heavenly-Dao rules set two locks for this: first, weight is not directly equal to decision power, only affecting voting weight, and everyone has a basic seat; second, weight dynamically rises and falls with rotation reminders, no civilization allowed to long top the chart. Higher-weight civilizations&#39; opinions matter more, but lower-weight civilizations&#39; opinions always have a channel to be heard. This design makes weight an incentive, not a new class — it guides civilizations to do more contribution, not to scramble for seat order.</p><p>Civilizational-weight assessment also has a floor design: even if a civilization&#39;s weight drops to zero due to force majeure, its basic seat and basic say are still retained. Weight measures &quot;contribution,&quot; not &quot;qualification to exist.&quot; A civilization temporarily unable to contribute is not kicked out of the Myriad-Rank assembly for low weight — it simply has smaller voting weight, but the door stays open, and weight naturally rebounds after it recovers. This dual track of &quot;contribution measurable, qualification not revoked&quot; is true republicanism.</p><p>This is the whole wisdom of weight design: incentivize upward, do not revoke existence.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational-weight assessment changes &quot;who decides&quot; from fists to contribution. Weight tilts toward those who lift Myriad Ranks, and civilization runs in the direction of lifting Myriad Ranks.</p><p>In the end, the Rule 29 described in this entry — civilizational-weight assessment — is no isolated case; it consistently points to the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s co-construction direction.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">Entry 29 · Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/918_模块5-第十七条-文明权重评估制.html">Entry 918 · Civilizational-Weight Assessment System</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/962_模块5-规则二十八-捷径心魔防范.html">Entry 962 · Rule 28 Shortcut Heart-Demon Prevention</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/964_模块5-规则三十-法则锚定权限普惠.html">Entry 964 · Rule 30 Law-Anchor Permission Universalization</a></li></ul>',27)])])}const m=e(n,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
